        "subject": "LU-9512 llite: Add O_TMPFILE support",
        "message": "LU-9512 llite: Add O_TMPFILE support\n\nThis patch adds VFS tmpfile (O_TMPFILE (nameless))\nfile support. The file will be automatically deleted\nwhen it is closed.\n\nVFS tmpfile (tmpfile) support which is little different\nfrom standard volatile file creation already present.\nWhile volatile file is either destroyed on close or\nswapped (migrate) but never link'ed. The tmpfile\nsupport via inode_operations->tmpfile can be linked\nand be brought out of orphan list and can be listed like\nregular file\n\ntmpfile uses unique (LUSTRE_VOLATILE_HDR + random) as\nname, same as volatile file. This is because, currently\nany file with such unique name is already put on\norphan (unlink, yet still open). Therefore tmpfile\npiggybacks on this already implemented feature to\nimplement tmpfiles. However, tmpfile and volatile\nfiles in Lustrefs is not same as mentioned above.\n\nTest is exercised against older 2.16 server also.\nNew sanity/63d test is added as verification.\nNew sanity/63e test is added as DNE verification.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial serverversion=2.17.0 testlist=sanity\nTest-Parameters: trivial serverversion=2.16.0 testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"63d 63e\"\nSigned-off-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\nChange-Id: I74b44bf2e4cfac10fef09d32679b104e83020b36\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/b2_15"
    }
